# Settings for the Tier-2 steps (model weights, video, stored detections).
#
# Tier 1 (`python run_tier1.py`) needs NONE of these: everything it reads is in data/.
#
# To use: copy this file to `.env` (same folder) and fill in the paths you have. Every line
# is optional. A script that needs a path you have not set stops with one sentence naming
# the missing input and the variable that locates it.
# docs/DATA_AVAILABILITY.md says what each location must contain and where to obtain it.

# Project data folder: stored detections and track tables for each season
# (deimv2_x_v27_corpus<year>/), the held-out test videos' detections (deimv2_x_v27_eval/),
# the video lists (label_batches/), the labelling database, the SAM2 cutout library.
# SALMONID_PROJECTS_ROOT=/path/to/Projects

# Raw RiverWatcher fishway video. The folder holds Ganaraska/ and Credit/ subfolders.
# SALMONID_FOOTAGE_ROOT=/path/to/RiverWatcher
# SALMONID_FOOTAGE_ROOT_FAST=/path/to/RiverWatcher      # optional faster copy of the same files
# SALMONID_RECOVERED_ROOT=/path/to/recovered            # the recovered 2020 Ganaraska archive

# Frozen training set (deimv2_fish_6class_masked_v26_clean/{train,val_clean}.json + images)
# SALMONID_COCO_CACHE=/path/to/ssl_cache

# The external DEIMv2 code at the pinned commit, with ckpts/ and outputs/ inside it
# (docs/DEIMV2_PIN.md). The published weights are expected at
# <SALMONID_DEIM_DIR>/outputs/deimv2_fish_x_v27/checkpoint0017.pth
# SALMONID_DEIM_DIR=/path/to/DEIMv2

# Technician count records for 2020 to 2023 (see docs/DATA_AVAILABILITY.md)
# SALMONID_LOMU_INTERVIEW_DIR=/path/to/lomu_interview
# SALMONID_MODEL_PRO_DIR=/path/to/model_pro

# Re-identification weights used by the BoT-SORT tracker. The tracking library downloads
# this file on first use if you leave the bare filename.
# SALMONID_REID_WEIGHTS=osnet_x0_25_msmt17.pt

# Optional phone notification when a long job ends (ntfy.sh). Off unless you set a topic.
# ntfy topics are public: choose a long, hard-to-guess name of your own.
# SALMONID_NTFY_TOPIC=

# Python interpreter of the DEIMv2 (GPU) environment, used by the training launcher and the
# corpus runner to start detection and training. Empty = the interpreter running the script.
# SALMONID_DEIM_PYTHON=/path/to/.venv_deim/bin/python

# The leak guard reads two exclusion lists: data/test_set_v6_holdout.json (in this repository)
# and <SALMONID_PROJECTS_ROOT>/label_batches/ls_test_set_v5.json (an older evaluation set that
# no manuscript number uses; external). If the second file is absent the guard stops, so that a
# missing list can never silently weaken it. Set this to 1 to continue with the lists you have.
# SALMONID_ALLOW_MISSING_HOLDOUT=1

# Less common Tier-2 locations (each has a default under SALMONID_PROJECTS_ROOT or external/)
# SALMONID_TECH_2025_DIR=/path/to/Riverwatcher_2025          # 2025 technician review exports
# SALMONID_BLIND_REVIEW_DIR=/path/to/blind_review_files      # the blind-review sample and record
# SALMONID_RECOVERED_2020_DATEMAP=/path/to/gan_recovered_datemap.json
# SALMONID_CLASSIFIER_CROPS=/path/to/crops_v1                # backbone comparison (Table S4)
# SALMONID_SPATIAL_DIR=/path/to/map_layers                   # Figure 1
